EXT. HIGH PLATEAU, BURNED FOREST - DAWN

Black trunks. Ash like grey snow. A crippled pickup with its hood up.

A man sits on its bumper, bandaging his hand. Another stands at the tree line, binoculars up. A third crouches by the tailgate, counting cans.

STRANGER
We can't stay.

TALL MAN
We can't leave.

STRANGER
We don't have fuel.

TALL MAN
We have legs.

WOMAN
(from the tailgate)
We have four cans of beans and no opener.

STRANGER
Then we use the knife.

WOMAN
It's your knife.

STRANGER
I know whose knife it is.

The tall man lowers the binoculars.

TALL MAN
Smoke. East ridge.

WOMAN
How far?

TALL MAN
Six miles.

STRANGER
It could be anyone.

TALL MAN
It could be the fire again.

WOMAN
It could be help.

STRANGER
It could be them.

A silence. They look at each other.

WOMAN
You never told us your name.

STRANGER
Elio.

WOMAN
Elio what?

ELIO
Just Elio.

TALL MAN
Okay, Just Elio. Here's what we do.

ELIO
(overlapping)
We split.

WOMAN
(overlapping)
We stay together.

^

TALL MAN
(overlapping both)
We go together, east, now!

A hiss in the trees. All three freeze. Branches crack. A shape moves in the ash, low and fast.

ELIO
Run!

The truck door slams. The woman dives. The tall man fires. A burst of gunshot echoes across the burned plateau, and the pale smoke rises, higher, higher.
